@floppyhammer I've a [pull request](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/46136) in flight to add more logging which should help with troubleshooting the issue.

If you're able to, can you patch PR #46136, enable verbose logging, and provide the resulting output logs.
If you don't know how to build the Godot editor from source, let me know and I can try to provide a generated binary.

@floppyhammer Thanks for the updated logs, they're showing where the issue starts!
On the second run, you can see in the logs that the engine starts processing some of the files generated by the first build:
```
Saving project files from res://android/build/build/intermediates/annotation_processor_list/debug/annotationProcessors.json into res://android/build/assets/android/build/build/intermediates/annotation_processor_list/debug/annotationProcessors.json
```

@akien-mga @Calinou Any idea why this could occur? There's a `.gdignore` file in the `android/build` folder so in theory it shouldn't be processed by the engine.

@floppyhammer @HEAVYPOLY Can you cherry-pick https://github.com/m4gr3d/godot/commit/78dacb7e489928c25797cc39ac0ba9de2253111c into your local Godot builds.

Once you have a build, reinstall the `android` folder by reinstalling the Android build template, then perform an export a couple of times with custom build enabled in order to generate and provide me with the relevant logs.

@floppyhammer This is similar to what you did before; with the extra logs I'm hoping to be able to track down where the Android directories and files are being added. As mentioned in the previous comment, in theory, the `.gdignore` should prevent that from happening, so there may a bug preventing that from happening.

@floppyhammer Thanks for the logs! It doesn't look like the `android` directory is being added as part of the indexing logic, so I'm struggling to see how it's added to the build process.. 

@floppyhammer Can you cherry-pick https://github.com/m4gr3d/godot/commit/8df3d5d01901afae5539a99b850b104b9fbf58b5 and perform the same steps as above. 
This commit attempts to fix the issue by hardcoding a filter for the `android` directory. This is only a workaround, but it should resolve the issue for the time being.

@akien-mga We may have to move the `android` directory outside of the `res://` directory to mitigate any future issues. Likely candidate could be the `data/settings` directory. Thoughts?

> I think there were errors related to .import files in android custom build.

@HEAVYPOLY For these errors, can you double-check the `.gdignore` file is in the `res://android/build` directory.
If it's, can you delete and reinstall the `android` directory and see if you can recreate the issue.
